    <!-- 7 — Governance -->
    <section class="docs-section">
      <h2 id="governance" class="docs-section-title">Governance</h2>
      <Callout tone="warning" title="Before you point this at anything that is not yours">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 0.6rem">
          <code>/design-sync</code> uploads component source and rendered previews. Three facts from
          Anthropic’s own admin guide for Team and Enterprise plans, as recorded here on 2026-08-26:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin: 0 0 0.6rem; padding-left: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7">
          <li>uploaded assets are stored <strong>persistently</strong> under enterprise retention;</li>
          <li>there is <strong>no data-residency support</strong>;</li>
          <li>Claude Design is <strong>default-off</strong> on Enterprise.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin: 0">
          Rehearsing on Atelier’s own open-source library is the safe case. Pushing an
          <strong>employer’s</strong> design system is a data-processing decision, not a tooling
          choice: route it to your organisation’s data-protection officer first, and organisation-level
          enablement to your information-security officer, before it reaches an agenda a client sees.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </section>

